───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COVERED SOFTWARE

  app_v1.py  —  Voice Studio Pro, Classic Edition  v1.0
  app_v2.py  —  Voice Studio, Production Edition   v2.0

Both editions are standalone Python/Tkinter desktop applications providing
speech-to-text (STT) and text-to-speech (TTS) functionality, authored by
Abhishek Srivastava.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

THIRD-PARTY ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS

This software makes use of the following open-source packages, each governed
by their own respective license:

  SpeechRecognition   BSD License
                      https://github.com/Uberi/speech_recognition
                      Used for Google Speech API integration (STT engine)
                      in both Classic and Premium editions.

  PyAudio             MIT License
                      https://people.csail.mit.edu/hubert/pyaudio/
                      Used for microphone access (PortAudio binding)
                      in both editions.

  pyttsx3             BSD License (2-Clause)
                      https://github.com/nateshmbhat/pyttsx3
                      Used for offline TTS (SAPI5 / espeak / nsss).
                      Both editions create a fresh engine instance per
                      speak call to avoid the known upstream COM / run-loop
                      re-entrancy bug.

  gTTS                MIT License
                      https://github.com/pndurette/gTTS
                      Used for online TTS and MP3 audio export.
                      Classic supports 16 locales; Premium supports 24.
                      Premium enforces an 8,000-character input limit.

  pygame              LGPL License (v2.1)
                      https://www.pygame.org/
                      Used for MP3 playback of gTTS output.
                      Both editions suppress pygame init banners safely.

  pydub               MIT License
                      https://github.com/jiaaro/pydub
                      Used for audio format conversion and fallback playback
                      when pygame is unavailable.

  PyInstaller         GPL License (v2) with Bootloader Exception
                      https://pyinstaller.org/
                      Used to package the application into standalone
                      executables. Not linked into the running application.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

GOOGLE SPEECH RECOGNITION API

Speech recognition in both editions is powered by the Google Speech
Recognition API (https://cloud.google.com/speech-to-text).

  · An active internet connection is required for all STT operations.
  · This software does not store, transmit, or share any audio data beyond
    what is required to perform recognition via the API.
  · Use of the API is subject to Google's Terms of Service:
    https://policies.google.com/terms

